@startuml

title Precedence of the levels: the statement a read of one datum uses

start

:a read names one datum and the level it acts for;

if (does the level hold a row for the key?) then (yes)
  :the level's row is the statement;
elseif (does a wider level hold one?) then (yes)
  :the wider level's row is the statement;
  note right
    The wider row stays where it lies.
    No level copies it and no level edits it.
  end note
else (no)
  :the datum is absent at every level;
  stop
endif

if (does the level state a difference over the wider row?) then (yes)
  :apply the level's row over the wider row;
  note right
    The overlay shape reads both rows.
    The wider row is still the statement
    of every key the level does not name.
  end note
endif

stop

@enduml
